  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\nIMPOSTER\\_LOG now works from the NuGet package (#135, closes #113). The package did not make the property visible to the generator, so setting it had no effect. The log is also more useful now:\n\nonce per compilation, the language version and whether the static Imposter() extensions are generated;\n\none line per imposter, with its generated file and target.\n\nSet IMPOSTER\\_LOG=true and build with -v:d to see the IMPLOG001 lines (see Getting Started).\n\nKeyword-named type parameters (#119, closes #109). Type parameters such as @class or @in were written without the @, so the generated file did not compile.\n\nAsync event callbacks run before handlers (#120, closes #110). Behaviour change: RaiseAsync now runs the Callback(...) callbacks before the subscribed handlers, the same order as Raise. Before, it awaited the handlers first.\n\nEvent verification messages name the event once (#124, closes #111). A failed subscription verification printed the event name twice. Message text change: update tests that assert on the exact text.\n\nNew diagnostic\n\nIMP006 (warning): closed generic target (#133, closes #112). Registering a closed generic type such as typeof(IRepository\\<User>) generates the same generic imposter as typeof(IRepository<>); the type arguments have no effect. The generator now warns and suggests the open registration. With TreatWarningsAsErrors, switch to the open registration or suppress IMP006.\n\nPackage\n\n37% smaller (#86, closes #85). The Roslyn 4.5, 4.7 and 4.11 generator builds were dropped because they compiled to the same code as the 4.4 build. Compilers 4.5–4.13 now load the 4.4 build. Generated code is unchanged.\n\nThe Roslyn 5.0 build uses the stable Microsoft.CodeAnalysis 5.0.0 (#84, closes #83) instead of a prerelease.\n\nInternal\n\nGenerator code cleanup, with byte-identical generated output (#89, #90, #92, #95, #96, #98, #100, #102, #104).",
